From 5dd764bbfc0c427ba7fee1b82f0af414d9b7c4ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Verbovoy <145046797+iverbovoy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:49:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] sfduo-layer-fx: a layer surface's look, drawn by phoc
 on its own frames

org.sfduo.Phoc.LayerEffect(namespace, target, duration) gives the layer
surfaces of a namespace an effect, animated from where it stands on the
output's frames; a newer request takes over from there. The dock's two
halves use it:

- corners per corner and an inset of the shape, drawn with a rounded-rect
  signed distance - a half squares its inner corners where it meets the
  other without repainting;
- alpha and dim;
- a squash of the width about an anchor (0.5 .. 1) - the half that is met
  gives against its screen edge;
- seamless: across the display's seam a surface is drawn up to where the
  seam starts and, past a tunnel an icon long, from where it ends; each part
  rounded at the seam, so it squeezes through rather than being sliced;
- merge: two merging surfaces side by side flow into each other across a
  gap of up to half the reach - a neck drawn over them by a smooth union of
  their shapes - with the region between them damaged as they move.

Works with Droidian's android renderer (legacy pass into the EGL window,
not flipped) and GLES2's buffer pass (flipped).
